<title>DENMARK: Maersk doubles African sailings.</title>
<headline>Maersk doubles African sailings.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish shipping and energy group A.P. Moeller's Maersk Line said on Tuesday that it was increasing its twice-monthly container vessel sailings between Europe and Africa to weekly services with immediate effect.</p>
<p>The service - which had been extended in response to customer demand - had originally been scheduled to start operating at a once-weekly frequency in the second half of 1997, Maersk said.</p>
<p>The container service sails from Algeciras, Spain to Durban and Capetown in South Africa, it said. --Chris Follett, Copenhagen newsroom +45-33969652</p>
